UTLIER_SUMMARY.csv\nSaved: slrdi_bhc_mahpi_nsr2db_paper_realtime5min_patientwise_ALL_TABLES.xlsx\nSaved: slrdi_bhc_mahpi_nsr2db_paper_realtime5min_patientwise_CONCLUSION.txt\nModel checkpoint: best_slrdi_bhc_mahpi_net.pt\n\nSLRDI-BHC-MAHPI-Net HRV Preservation Conclusion\n\nModel:\nSelf-Learning RR-Difference Interpolation\n+ Bias-Corrected HRV-Constrained Mask-Aware Physiological Imputation Network\nTCN + Transformer + BiLSTM\n\nDataset:\nNormal Sinus Rhythm RR Interval Database\n\nMissing type:\npaper_realtime_5min\n\nMissing rate:\n0.2\n\nRepeated masks per record:\n5\n\nValidation HRV calibration applied:\nTrue\n\nPointwise missing RR reconstruction:\nN missing points: 197038\nMAE_norm: 0.09970599\nMSE_norm: 0.05162258\nRMSE_norm: 0.22720603\nR2_norm: 0.94633017\nMAE_seconds: 0.01672597\nRMSE_seconds: 0.03811447\nMAE_ms: 16.7260\nRMSE_ms: 38.1145\nMSE_ms2: 1452.7127\nMean relative error percent: 2.3271\nMedian relative error percent: 1.4140\nMAPE percent: 2.3271\nP95 absolute error ms: 45.4840\nP99 absolute error ms: 106.4299\nMaximum absolute error ms used for evaluation: 1916.0656\nRaw maximum absolute error before physiological clipping: 1916.0656\nClipped maximum absolute error: 1916.0656\nRaw percent error > 100 ms: 1.0820\nClipped percent error > 100 ms: 1.0820\n\nPaired t-test not statistically different:\n7 / 9\n\nTOST equivalent:\n9 / 9\n\nFinal preserved:\n9 / 9\n\nInterpretation:\nThe self-learning interpolation module learns RR-difference and local rhythm patterns\nfrom artificially masked training data. The true hidden RR values are used as targets.\nDuring testing, the trained model estimates missing RR intervals in unseen records.\n\nThe paired t-test evaluates whether the mean TRUE-vs-IMPUTED difference is exactly zero.\nThe TOST equivalence test evaluates whether the difference is within practical equivalence bounds.\n\nThe desired strongest result is:\n    paired t-test = not statistically different\n    TOST = equivalent\n\nA still scientifically valid result is:\n    paired t-test = statistically different\n    TOST = equivalent\n\nThat means the difference is statistically detectable but practically negligible.\n\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1500x500 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":3},{"cell_type":"code","source":"","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# 30% missing","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# SLRDI-BHC-MAHPI-Net\n# Self-Learning RR-Difference Interpolation\n# + Bias-Corrected HRV-Constrained Mask-Aware Imputation Network\n#\n# For Normal Sinus Rhythm RR Interval Database\n#\n# Main ideas:\n#   1. Artificially hide RR intervals during training.\n#   2. Self-learning interpolation module learns RR rhythm/difference patterns.\n#   3. BHC-MAHPI-Net refines the interpolated signal.\n#   4. Output replaces only missing RR values; observed RR values remain unchanged.\n#   5. Evaluates MAE, RMSE, R2, relative error in ms and %.\n#   6. Performs patientwise HRV paired t-test and TOST equivalence testing.\n#   7. Detects, saves, visualizes, and reduces extreme imputation outliers.\n# ============================================================\n\n!pip install wfdb statsmodels openpyxl -q\n\nimport os\nimport random\nimport warnings\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport wfdb\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom scipy import signal\nfrom scipy.stats import ttest_rel, t\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\nfrom sklearn.metrics import mean_absolute_error, mean_squared_error, r2_score\nfrom statsmodels.stats.multitest import multipletests\n\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nfrom torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\n\nfrom tqdm import tqdm\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n\n# ============================================================\n# 1. CONFIGURATION\n# ============================================================\n\nSEED = 42\nrandom.seed(SEED)\nnp.random.seed(SEED)\ntorch.manual_seed(SEED)\n\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n    torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(SEED)\n\nDEVICE = \"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\nprint(\"Using device:\", DEVICE)\n\nFS = 128.0\n\n# Physiological RR range used consistently in loading, evaluation, inference, and clipping.\nPHYS_RR_MIN_SEC = 0.25\nPHYS_RR_MAX_SEC = 2.50\n\nWINDOW_SIZE = 256\nSTRIDE = 128\nMAIN_MISSING_RATE = 0.30  # paper-style experiment: 10% missing; change to 0.20, 0.30, ..., 0.70 for other runs\n\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\nEPOCHS = 50\nLR = 1e-3\nWEIGHT_DECAY = 1e-4\n\nTRAIN_MISSING_TYPE = \"mixed\"       # random, burst, gilbert, mixed\nVAL_MISSING_TYPE = \"random\"\n# Window-level test loader still uses random masks for quick validation/outlier visualization.\nTEST_WINDOW_MISSING_TYPE = \"random\"\n# Final pointwise + patientwise HRV evaluation uses the paper missing-value procedure.\nTEST_MISSING_TYPE = \"paper_realtime_5min\"\n\n# Outlier handling\nAPPLY_PHYSIOLOGICAL_CLIP_IN_EVAL = True\nOUTLIER_ERROR_THRESHOLD_MS = 100.0\nEXTREME_OUTLIER_THRESHOLD_MS = 500.0\nOUTLIER_LOSS_WEIGHT = 0.20\nHUBER_LOSS_WEIGHT = 0.30\nHUBER_DELTA_NORM = 0.50\n\n# Optional two-stage training\nUSE_SLRDI_PRETRAIN = True\nSLRDI_PRETRAIN_EPOCHS = 15\n\nHRV_REPEATS = 5\nAPPLY_HRV_CALIBRATION = True\n\nRESULTS_DIR = Path(\"/kaggle/working/results_slrdi_bhc_mahpi\")\nRESULTS_DIR.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n\nHRV_RESULTS_DIR = Path(\"/kaggle/working/hrv_results_slrdi_bhc_mahpi\")\nHRV_RESULTS_DIR.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n\nHRV_PREFIX = \"slrdi_bhc_mahpi_nsr2db_paper_realtime5min_patientwise\"\n\nHRV_METRICS = [\n    \"meanNN (s)\",\n    \"HR (bpm)\",\n    \"SDNN (ms)\",\n    \"RMSSD (ms)\",\n    \"pNN50 (%)\",\n    \"VLF (%)\",\n    \"LF (%)\",\n    \"HF (%)\",\n    \"LF/HF\"\n]\n\n# ============================================================\n# 2. DATASET DISCOVERY\n# ============================================================\n\ndef find_dataset_path():\n    input_root = Path(\"/kaggle/input\")\n\n    print(\"Available Kaggle input folders:\")\n    for path in input_root.iterdir():\n        print(\" -\", path)\n\n    for folder in input_root.iterdir():\n        if (folder / \"RECORDS\").exists():\n            return folder\n        for sub in folder.rglob(\"RECORDS\"):\n            return sub.parent\n\n    raise FileNotFoundError(\"Could not find RECORDS file in /kaggle/input.\")\n\n\ndef read_records_file(data_dir):\n    records_path = data_dir / \"RECORDS\"\n    with open(records_path, \"r\") as f:\n        records = [line.strip() for line in f.readlines() if line.strip()]\n    return records\n\nDATA_DIR = find_dataset_path()\nrecords = read_records_file(DATA_DIR)\n\nprint(\"\\nUsing dataset path:\", DATA_DIR)\nprint(\"Total records found:\", len(records))\nprint(\"First 10 records:\", records[:10])\n\n# ============================================================\n# 3. LOAD RR INTERVALS FROM WFDB ANNOTATIONS\n# ============================================================\n\ndef load_rr_from_annotation(record_name, data_dir, fs=128.0):\n    \"\"\"\n    NSR RR Interval Database loader.\n    The .ecg file is read as the WFDB annotation extension.\n    RR = diff(annotation_samples) / fs.\n    \"\"\"\n    record_path = str(data_dir / record_name)\n\n    try:\n        ann = wfdb.rdann(record_path, \"ecg\")\n        samples = np.asarray(ann.sample, dtype=np.float64)\n\n        if len(samples) < 3:\n            return None\n\n        rr = np.diff(samples) / fs\n        rr = rr[np.isfinite(rr)]\n        rr = rr[(rr > PHYS_RR_MIN_SEC) & (rr < PHYS_RR_MAX_SEC)]\n\n        if len(rr) <= WINDOW_SIZE:\n            return None\n\n        return rr.astype(np.float32)\n\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Could not read {record_name}: {e}\")\n        return None\n\n\ndef load_all_rr_sequences(data_dir):\n    all_rr = {}\n\n    for rec in records:\n        rr = load_rr_from_annotation(rec, data_dir, fs=FS)\n        if rr is not None and len(rr) > WINDOW_SIZE:\n            all_rr[rec] = rr\n            print(f\"{rec}: loaded {len(rr)} RR intervals\")\n        else:\n            print(f\"{rec}: skipped\")\n\n    return all_rr\n\nprint(\"\\nLoading RR sequences...\")\nall_rr = load_all_rr_sequences(DATA_DIR)\nprint(\"\\nTotal valid records:\", len(all_rr))\n\nif len(all_rr) == 0:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"No RR records loaded. Check dataset files and annotation extension.\")\n\n# ============================================================\n# 4. WINDOW CREATION\n# ============================================================\n\ndef create_windows(rr_sequence, window_size=256, stride=128):\n    windows = []\n    for start in range(0, len(rr_sequence) - window_size + 1, stride):\n        w = rr_sequence[start:start + window_size]\n        if np.all(np.isfinite(w)):\n            windows.append(w)\n    return windows\n\n\ndef build_window_dataset(all_rr):\n    windows = []\n    record_ids = []\n\n    for rec, rr in all_rr.items():\n        rec_windows = create_windows(rr, WINDOW_SIZE, STRIDE)\n        windows.extend(rec_windows)\n        record_ids.extend([rec] * len(rec_windows))\n\n    return np.array(windows, dtype=np.float32), np.array(record_ids)\n\nwindows, record_ids = build_window_dataset(all_rr)\n\nprint(\"\\nTotal windows:\", len(windows))\nprint(\"Window shape:\", windows.shape)\nprint(\"Unique records:\", len(np.unique(record_ids)))\n\nif len(windows) == 0:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"No valid windows created.\")\n\n# ============================================================\n# 5. RECORD-LEVEL SPLIT\n# ============================================================\n\nunique_records = np.unique(record_ids)\n\ntrain_records, test_records = train_test_split(\n    unique_records,\n    test_size=0.15,\n    random_state=SEED\n)\n\ntrain_records, val_records = train_test_split(\n    train_records,\n    test_size=0.15,\n    random_state=SEED\n)\n\ntrain_windows_raw = windows[np.isin(record_ids, train_records)]\nval_windows_raw = windows[np.isin(record_ids, val_records)]\ntest_windows_raw = windows[np.isin(record_ids, test_records)]\n\ntrain_window_record_ids = record_ids[np.isin(record_ids, train_records)]\nval_window_record_ids = record_ids[np.isin(record_ids, val_records)]\ntest_window_record_ids = record_ids[np.isin(record_ids, test_records)]\n\nprint(\"\\nRecord split:\")\nprint(\"Train records:\", len(train_records))\nprint(\"Validation records:\", len(val_records))\nprint(\"Test records:\", len(test_records))\n\nprint(\"\\nWindow split:\")\nprint(\"Train windows:\", len(train_windows_raw))\nprint(\"Validation windows:\", len(val_windows_raw))\nprint(\"Test windows:\", len(test_windows_raw))\n\n\ndef subset_all_rr(all_rr, selected_records):\n    return {rec: all_rr[rec] for rec in selected_records if rec in all_rr}\n\ntrain_all_rr = subset_all_rr(all_rr, train_records)\nval_all_rr = subset_all_rr(all_rr, val_records)\ntest_all_rr = subset_all_rr(all_rr, test_records)\n\n# ============================================================\n# 6. NORMALIZATION\n# ============================================================\n\ndef normalize_windows(train_windows, val_windows, test_windows):\n    mean = train_windows.mean()\n    std = train_windows.std() + 1e-8\n    train_norm = (train_windows - mean) / std\n    val_norm = (val_windows - mean) / std\n    test_norm = (test_windows - mean) / std\n    return train_norm.astype(np.float32), val_norm.astype(np.float32), test_norm.astype(np.float32), float(mean), float(std)\n\ntrain_windows, val_windows, test_windows, rr_mean, rr_std = normalize_windows(\n    train_windows_raw,\n    val_windows_raw,\n    test_windows_raw\n)\n\nprint(\"\\nNormalization:\")\nprint(\"RR mean seconds:\", rr_mean)\nprint(\"RR std seconds:\", rr_std)\nprint(\"RR std milliseconds:\", rr_std * 1000.0)\n\n# ============================================================\n# 7. MISSINGNESS GENERATION\n# ============================================================\n\ndef apply_random_missing(x, missing_rate=0.05):\n    mask = np.ones_like(x, dtype=np.float32)\n    n_missing = max(1, int(len(x) * missing_rate))\n    missing_idx = np.random.choice(len(x), n_missing, replace=False)\n    mask[missing_idx] = 0.0\n    x_missing = x.copy()\n    x_missing[missing_idx] = 0.0\n    return x_missing.astype(np.float32), mask.astype(np.float32)\n\n\ndef apply_burst_missing(x, missing_rate=0.05):\n    mask = np.ones_like(x, dtype=np.float32)\n    n_missing = max(1, int(len(x) * missing_rate))\n    burst_len = min(n_missing, random.randint(3, max(3, n_missing)))\n    start = random.randint(0, len(x) - burst_len)\n    mask[start:start + burst_len] = 0.0\n    x_missing = x.copy()\n    x_missing[mask == 0] = 0.0\n    return x_missing.astype(np.float32), mask.astype(np.float32)\n\n\ndef apply_gilbert_missing(x, missing_rate=0.05, mean_burst_length=10):\n    n = len(x)\n    p_exit = 1.0 / mean_burst_length\n    missing_rate = min(missing_rate, 0.99)\n    p_enter = (missing_rate / (1.0 - missing_rate)) * p_exit\n    p_enter = min(max(p_enter, 0.0001), 0.99)\n    p_exit = min(max(p_exit, 0.0001), 0.99)\n\n    mask = np.ones(n, dtype=np.float32)\n    state = 0\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        if state == 0:\n            if random.random() < p_enter:\n                state = 1\n        else:\n            if random.random() < p_exit:\n                state = 0\n        if state == 1:\n            mask[i] = 0.0\n\n    if np.sum(mask == 0) == 0:\n        idx = np.random.choice(n, max(1, int(n * missing_rate)), replace=False)\n        mask[idx] = 0.0\n\n    x_missing = x.copy()\n    x_missing[mask == 0] = 0.0\n    return x_missing.astype(np.float32), mask.astype(np.float32)\n\n\ndef apply_mixed_missing(x, missing_rate=0.05):\n    r = random.random()\n    if r < 0.33:\n        return apply_random_missing(x, missing_rate)\n    elif r < 0.66:\n        return apply_burst_missing(x, missing_rate)\n    else:\n        return apply_gilbert_missing(x, missing_rate)\n\n\ndef apply_missing(x, missing_rate=0.05, missing_type=\"random\"):\n    if missing_type == \"random\":\n        return apply_random_missing(x, missing_rate)\n    elif missing_type == \"burst\":\n        return apply_burst_missing(x, missing_rate)\n    elif missing_type == \"gilbert\":\n        return apply_gilbert_missing(x, missing_rate)\n    elif missing_type == \"mixed\":\n        return apply_mixed_missing(x, missing_rate)\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(\"missing_type must be random, burst, gilbert, mixed. Paper-style missingness is applied on full RR sequences only.\")\n\n\ndef apply_paper_realtime_5min_missing_mask(\n    rr_seconds,\n    missing_rate=0.10,\n    window_sec=300.0,\n    step_sec=60.0,\n    edge_margin_beats=2,\n    seed=None\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Paper-style missing-value procedure.\n\n    This follows the real-time HRV interpolation paper:\n        - split the full RR/IBI signal into 5-minute windows\n        - use 4-minute overlap\n        - slide by 1 minute\n        - keep missing values already created in the overlap\n        - delete only enough additional RR intervals from the new last 1 minute\n        - each 5-minute HRV window has approximately the target missing percentage\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    rr_seconds : array-like\n        Complete RR intervals in seconds.\n    missing_rate : float\n        Fraction of missing values, e.g., 0.10 for 10%.\n    window_sec : float\n        HRV analysis window length. Paper uses 300 s = 5 min.\n    step_sec : float\n        Sliding step. Paper uses 60 s = 1 min, therefore 4 min overlap.\n    edge_margin_beats : int\n        Avoid deleting first/last few beats of each candidate segment to reduce\n        interpolation/extrapolation problems.\n    seed : int or None\n        Random seed for reproducible masks.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    mask : np.ndarray\n        1 = observed, 0 = missing.\n    \"\"\"\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n\n    rr_seconds = np.asarray(rr_seconds, dtype=np.float32)\n    n = len(rr_seconds)\n\n    mask = np.ones(n, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    if n < 3:\n        return mask\n\n    beat_times = np.cumsum(rr_seconds)\n    beat_times = beat_times - beat_times[0]\n    total_duration = float(beat_times[-1])\n\n    # If the sequence is shorter than 5 minutes, use simple random deletion.\n    if total_duration < window_sec:\n        n_missing = max(1, int(round(n * missing_rate)))\n        if n > 2 * edge_margin_beats:\n            candidates = np.arange(edge_margin_beats, n - edge_margin_beats)\n        else:\n            candidates = np.arange(n)\n        n_missing = min(n_missing, len(candidates))\n        if n_missing > 0:\n            missing_idx = rng.choice(candidates, size=n_missing, replace=False)\n            mask[missing_idx] = 0.0\n        return mask.astype(np.float32)\n\n    start_time = 0.0\n    first_window = True\n\n    while start_time + window_sec <= total_duration:\n        end_time = start_time + window_sec\n        overlap_end = start_time + (window_sec - step_sec)  # first 4 minutes\n\n        window_idx = np.where((beat_times >= start_time) & (beat_times < end_time))[0]\n\n        if len(window_idx) == 0:\n            start_time += step_sec\n            first_window = False\n            continue\n\n        target_missing = int(round(len(window_idx) * missing_rate))\n\n        if first_window:\n            # First 5-min window: randomly delete target_missing from the whole window.\n            candidates = window_idx.copy()\n            if len(candidates) > 2 * edge_margin_beats:\n                candidates = candidates[edge_margin_beats:-edge_margin_beats]\n\n            n_delete = min(target_missing, len(candidates))\n            if n_delete > 0:\n                delete_idx = rng.choice(candidates, size=n_delete, replace=False)\n                mask[delete_idx] = 0.0\n\n        else:\n            # Later windows: overlap already contains missing values from previous windows.\n            overlap_idx = np.where((beat_times >= start_time) & (beat_times < overlap_end))[0]\n            n_overlap_missing = int(np.sum(mask[overlap_idx] == 0.0))\n\n            # Delete only enough from the new last 1-minute segment.\n            n_new_delete = target_missing - n_overlap_missing\n\n            last_minute_idx = np.where(\n                (beat_times >= overlap_end) &\n                (beat_times < end_time) &\n                (mask == 1.0)\n            )[0]\n\n            if len(last_minute_idx) > 2 * edge_margin_beats:\n                last_minute_idx = last_minute_idx[edge_margin_beats:-edge_margin_beats]\n\n            n_new_delete = max(0, min(n_new_delete, len(last_minute_idx)))\n\n            if n_new_delete > 0:\n                delete_idx = rng.choice(last_minute_idx, size=n_new_delete, replace=False)\n                mask[delete_idx] = 0.0\n\n        start_time += step_sec\n        first_window = False\n\n    return mask.astype(np.float32)\n\n# ============================================================\n# 8. SELF-LEARNING FEATURES\n# ============================================================\n\ndef rr_difference_feature(x):\n    \"\"\"\n    First-order RR difference feature.\n    This gives the model explicit local rhythm-change information.\n    \"\"\"\n    x = np.asarray(x, dtype=np.float32)\n    d = np.zeros_like(x, dtype=np.float32)\n    d[1:] = x[1:] - x[:-1]\n    d[0] = 0.0\n    return d.astype(np.float32)\n\n\ndef rr_local_slope_feature(x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Central-difference local slope feature.\n    \"\"\"\n    x = np.asarray(x, dtype=np.float32)\n    s = np.zeros_like(x, dtype=np.float32)\n    if len(x) > 2:\n        s[1:-1] = 0.5 * (x[2:] - x[:-2])\n        s[0] = x[1] - x[0]\n        s[-1] = x[-1] - x[-2]\n    return s.astype(np.float32)\n\n\ndef rr_local_mean_feature(x, window=9):\n    x = np.asarray(x, dtype=np.float32)\n    out = np.zeros_like(x, dtype=np.float32)\n    half = window // 2\n    for i in range(len(x)):\n        left = max(0, i - half)\n        right = min(len(x), i + half + 1)\n        out[i] = np.mean(x[left:right])\n    return out.astype(np.float32)\n\n# ============================================================\n# 9. DATASET AND DATALOADERS\n# ============================================================\n\nclass RRImputationDataset(Dataset):\n    \"\"\"\n    Input channels:\n        0 corrupted RR sequence, zero-filled at missing positions\n        1 binary mask, 1 observed and 0 missing\n        2 RR first-difference feature from corrupted sequence\n        3 local slope feature from corrupted sequence\n        4 local mean feature from corrupted sequence\n\n    Target:\n        complete normalized RR sequence\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, windows, missing_rate=0.05, missing_type=\"random\", window_record_ids=None):\n        self.windows = windows.astype(np.float32)\n        self.missing_rate = missing_rate\n        self.missing_type = missing_type\n        self.window_record_ids = window_record_ids\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        return len(self.windows)\n\n    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n        y = self.windows[idx]\n\n        x_missing, mask = apply_missing(\n            y,\n            missing_rate=self.missing_rate,\n            missing_type=self.missing_type\n        )\n\n        diff = rr_difference_feature(x_missing)\n        slope = rr_local_slope_feature(x_missing)\n        local_mean = rr_local_mean_feature(x_missing, window=9)\n\n        x = np.stack([x_missing, mask, diff, slope, local_mean], axis=0)\n\n        return (\n            torch.tensor(x, dtype=torch.float32),\n            torch.tensor(y, dtype=torch.float32),\n            torch.tensor(mask, dtype=torch.float32)\n        )\n\ntrain_ds = RRImputationDataset(train_windows, MAIN_MISSING_RATE, TRAIN_MISSING_TYPE, train_window_record_ids)\nval_ds = RRImputationDataset(val_windows, MAIN_MISSING_RATE, VAL_MISSING_TYPE, val_window_record_ids)\ntest_ds = RRImputationDataset(test_windows, MAIN_MISSING_RATE, TEST_WINDOW_MISSING_TYPE, test_window_record_ids)\n\ntrain_loader = DataLoader(train_ds, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=True, num_workers=2, pin_memory=True)\nval_loader = DataLoader(val_ds, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=False, num_workers=2, pin_memory=True)\ntest_loader = DataLoader(test_ds, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=False, num_workers=2, pin_memory=True)\n\nsample_x, sample_y, sample_mask = next(iter(train_loader))\nprint(\"\\nSample batch:\")\nprint(\"Input shape:\", sample_x.shape)\nprint(\"Target shape:\", sample_y.shape)\nprint(\"Mask shape:\", sample_mask.shape)\n\n# ============================================================\n# 10. MODEL: SLRDI + BHC-MAHPI-NET\n# ============================================================\n\nclass PositionalEncoding(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, d_model, max_len=5000):\n        super().__init__()\n        pe = torch.zeros(max_len, d_model)\n        position = torch.arange(0, max_len).float().unsqueeze(1)\n        div_term = torch.exp(torch.arange(0, d_model, 2).float() * (-np.log(10000.0) / d_model))\n        pe[:, 0::2] = torch.sin(position * div_term)\n        if d_model % 2 == 1:\n            pe[:, 1::2] = torch.cos(position * div_term[:-1])\n        else:\n            pe[:, 1::2] = torch.cos(position * div_term)\n        pe = pe.unsqueeze(0)\n        self.register_buffer(\"pe\", pe)\n\n    def forward(self, x):\n        return x + self.pe[:, :x.size(1), :]\n\n\nclass TCNBlock(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, in_channels, out_channels, kernel_size=5, dilation=1, dropout=0.1):\n        super().__init__()\n        padding = (kernel_size - 1) * dilation // 2\n\n        self.net = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Conv1d(in_channels, out_channels, kernel_size=kernel_size, padding=padding, dilation=dilation),\n            nn.BatchNorm1d(out_channels),\n            nn.ReLU(),\n            nn.Dropout(dropout),\n            nn.Conv1d(out_channels, out_channels, kernel_size=kernel_size, padding=padding, dilation=dilation),\n            nn.BatchNorm1d(out_channels),\n            nn.ReLU(),\n            nn.Dropout(dropout)\n        )\n\n        self.residual = nn.Conv1d(in_channels, out_channels, kernel_size=1) if in_channels != out_channels else nn.Identity()\n\n    def forward(self, x):\n        return self.net(x) + self.residual(x)\n\n\nclass SelfLearningRRDifferenceInterpolation(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Self-learning interpolation block.\n\n    It learns from:\n        corrupted RR\n        mask\n        RR difference\n        local slope\n        local mean\n\n    It predicts an initial full RR sequence.\n    Observed values are kept unchanged:\n        filled = mask * observed + (1-mask) * learned_prediction\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, in_channels=5, hidden=64, dropout=0.05):\n        super().__init__()\n\n        self.net = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Conv1d(in_channels, hidden, kernel_size=7, padding=3),\n            nn.BatchNorm1d(hidden),\n            nn.ReLU(),\n            nn.Dropout(dropout),\n\n            nn.Conv1d(hidden, hidden, kernel_size=7, padding=3, dilation=1),\n            nn.BatchNorm1d(hidden),\n            nn.ReLU(),\n            nn.Dropout(dropout),\n\n            nn.Conv1d(hidden, hidden, kernel_size=5, padding=4, dilation=2),\n            nn.BatchNorm1d(hidden),\n            nn.ReLU(),\n            nn.Dropout(dropout),\n\n            nn.Conv1d(hidden, hidden, kernel_size=5, padding=8, dilation=4),\n            nn.BatchNorm1d(hidden),\n            nn.ReLU(),\n            nn.Dropout(dropout),\n\n            nn.Conv1d(hidden, 1, kernel_size=1)\n        )\n\n    def forward(self, x):\n        corrupted_rr = x[:, 0, :]\n        mask = x[:, 1, :]\n\n        learned_pred = self.net(x).squeeze(1)\n\n        # Keep observed RR unchanged, replace only missing RR.\n        filled = mask * corrupted_rr + (1.0 - mask) * learned_pred\n\n        return filled, learned_pred\n\n\nclass BHC_MAHPINet_Backbone(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    BHC-MAHPI refinement backbone.\n    Input channels:\n        0 self-learned interpolated RR\n        1 mask\n        2 RR difference of interpolated RR\n        3 local slope of interpolated RR\n        4 local mean of interpolated RR\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, seq_len=256, in_channels=5, d_model=64, nhead=4, num_transformer_layers=2, lstm_hidden=64, dropout=0.1):\n        super().__init__()\n\n        self.tcn = nn.Sequential(\n            TCNBlock(in_channels, d_model, kernel_size=5, dilation=1, dropout=dropout),\n            TCNBlock(d_model, d_model, kernel_size=5, dilation=2, dropout=dropout),\n            TCNBlock(d_model, d_model, kernel_size=5, dilation=4, dropout=dropout)\n        )\n\n        self.pos_encoder = PositionalEncoding(d_model, max_len=seq_len)\n\n        encoder_layer = nn.TransformerEncoderLayer(\n            d_model=d_model,\n            nhead=nhead,\n            dim_feedforward=128,\n            dropout=dropout,\n            batch_first=True,\n            activation=\"gelu\"\n        )\n\n        self.transformer = nn.TransformerEncoder(encoder_layer, num_layers=num_transformer_layers)\n\n        self.bilstm = nn.LSTM(\n            input_size=d_model,\n            hidden_size=lstm_hidden,\n            num_layers=1,\n            batch_first=True,\n            bidirectional=True\n        )\n\n        self.fusion = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Linear(d_model + 2 * lstm_hidden, 128),\n            nn.ReLU(),\n            nn.Dropout(dropout),\n            nn.Linear(128, 1)\n        )\n\n    def forward(self, x):\n        local_feat = self.tcn(x)\n        local_feat = local_feat.permute(0, 2, 1)\n        trans_in = self.pos_encoder(local_feat)\n        trans_feat = self.transformer(trans_in)\n        lstm_feat, _ = self.bilstm(trans_feat)\n        fused = torch.cat([trans_feat, lstm_feat], dim=-1)\n        out = self.fusion(fused).squeeze(-1)\n        return out\n\n\nclass SLRDI_BHC_MAHPINet(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Full proposed model.\n\n    Stage 1:\n        Self-learning RR-difference interpolation.\n    Stage 2:\n        HRV-constrained BHC-MAHPI refinement.\n\n    Final output keeps observed RR fixed:\n        final = mask * observed + (1-mask) * refined_prediction\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, seq_len=256, d_model=64, nhead=4, num_transformer_layers=2, lstm_hidden=64, dropout=0.1):\n        super().__init__()\n\n        self.slrdi = SelfLearningRRDifferenceInterpolation(\n            in_channels=5,\n            hidden=64,\n            dropout=0.05\n        )\n\n        self.backbone = BHC_MAHPINet_Backbone(\n            seq_len=seq_len,\n            in_channels=5,\n            d_model=d_model,\n            nhead=nhead,\n            num_transformer_layers=num_transformer_layers,\n            lstm_hidden=lstm_hidden,\n            dropout=dropout\n        )\n\n    def make_refinement_input(self, filled, mask):\n        # Torch differentiable local features from filled sequence.\n        diff = torch.zeros_like(filled)\n        diff[:, 1:] = filled[:, 1:] - filled[:, :-1]\n\n        slope = torch.zeros_like(filled)\n        slope[:, 1:-1] = 0.5 * (filled[:, 2:] - filled[:, :-2])\n        slope[:, 0] = filled[:, 1] - filled[:, 0]\n        slope[:, -1] = filled[:, -1] - filled[:, -2]\n\n        # Local mean with average pooling.\n        local_mean = nn.functional.avg_pool1d(\n            filled.unsqueeze(1),\n            kernel_size=9,\n            stride=1,\n            padding=4\n        ).squeeze(1)\n\n        return torch.stack([filled, mask, diff, slope, local_mean], dim=1)\n\n    def forward(self, x, return_intermediate=False):\n        corrupted_rr = x[:, 0, :]\n        mask = x[:, 1, :]\n\n        slrdi_filled, slrdi_raw = self.slrdi(x)\n\n        refinement_input = self.make_refinement_input(slrdi_filled, mask)\n        refined_pred = self.backbone(refinement_input)\n\n        # Keep observed values unchanged.\n        final = mask * corrupted_rr + (1.0 - mask) * refined_pred\n\n        if return_intermediate:\n            return final, slrdi_filled, slrdi_raw\n\n        return final\n\n# ============================================================\n# 11. DIFFERENTIABLE HRV FEATURES AND LOSS\n# ============================================================\n\nRR_MEAN_T = torch.tensor(rr_mean, dtype=torch.float32, device=DEVICE)\nRR_STD_T = torch.tensor(rr_std, dtype=torch.float32, device=DEVICE)\n\n\ndef denormalize_rr_torch(rr_norm):\n    return rr_norm * RR_STD_T + RR_MEAN_T\n\n\ndef normalize_rr_torch(rr_sec):\n    return (rr_sec - RR_MEAN_T) / (RR_STD_T + 1e-8)\n\n\ndef physiological_clip_norm_numpy(rr_norm, rr_mean, rr_std, low=PHYS_RR_MIN_SEC, high=PHYS_RR_MAX_SEC):\n    \"\"\"Clip normalized RR predictions after converting them to seconds, then return normalized values.\"\"\"\n    rr_sec = rr_norm * rr_std + rr_mean\n    rr_sec = np.clip(rr_sec, low, high)\n    return ((rr_sec - rr_mean) / (rr_std + 1e-8)).astype(np.float32)\n\n\ndef physiological_clip_norm_torch(rr_norm, low=PHYS_RR_MIN_SEC, high=PHYS_RR_MAX_SEC):\n    \"\"\"Torch version used when a differentiable physiological range is needed.\"\"\"\n    rr_sec = denormalize_rr_torch(rr_norm)\n    rr_sec = torch.clamp(rr_sec, low, high)\n    return normalize_rr_torch(rr_sec)\n\n\ndef differentiable_hrv_features(rr_norm):\n    rr_sec = denormalize_rr_torch(rr_norm)\n    rr_sec = torch.clamp(rr_sec, PHYS_RR_MIN_SEC, PHYS_RR_MAX_SEC)\n    rr_ms = rr_sec * 1000.0\n\n    mean_nn = torch.mean(rr_sec, dim=1)\n    hr = 60.0 / (mean_nn + 1e-8)\n    sdnn = torch.std(rr_ms, dim=1)\n\n    diff_ms = rr_ms[:, 1:] - rr_ms[:, :-1]\n    rmssd = torch.sqrt(torch.mean(diff_ms ** 2, dim=1) + 1e-8)\n\n    tau = 5.0\n    soft_nn50 = torch.sigmoid((torch.abs(diff_ms) - 50.0) / tau)\n    soft_pnn50 = torch.mean(soft_nn50, dim=1) * 100.0\n\n    return torch.stack([mean_nn, hr, sdnn, rmssd, soft_pnn50], dim=1)\n\n\ndef masked_mae_loss(pred, target, mask):\n    missing = 1.0 - mask\n    return (torch.abs(pred - target) * missing).sum() / (missing.sum() + 1e-8)\n\n\ndef masked_mse_loss(pred, target, mask):\n    missing = 1.0 - mask\n    return (((pred - target) ** 2) * missing).sum() / (missing.sum() + 1e-8)\n\n\ndef masked_huber_loss(pred, target, mask, delta=HUBER_DELTA_NORM):\n    \"\"\"Huber loss on missing positions. It is more robust than pure MSE.\"\"\"\n    missing = 1.0 - mask\n    error = pred - target\n    abs_error = torch.abs(error)\n    delta_t = torch.tensor(delta, dtype=pred.dtype, device=pred.device)\n    quadratic = torch.minimum(abs_error, delta_t)\n    linear = abs_error - quadratic\n    huber = 0.5 * quadratic ** 2 + delta_t * linear\n    return (huber * missing).sum() / (missing.sum() + 1e-8)\n\n\ndef outlier_penalty_loss(pred, target, mask, threshold_ms=OUTLIER_ERROR_THRESHOLD_MS):\n    \"\"\"Extra penalty only for missing-position errors larger than threshold_ms.\"\"\"\n    missing = 1.0 - mask\n    pred_sec = denormalize_rr_torch(pred)\n    target_sec = denormalize_rr_torch(target)\n    abs_error_ms = torch.abs(pred_sec - target_sec) * 1000.0\n    excess_ms = torch.relu(abs_error_ms - threshold_ms)\n    return (excess_ms * missing).sum() / (missing.sum() + 1e-8) / 1000.0\n\n\ndef observed_consistency_loss(pred, target, mask):\n    return (torch.abs(pred - target) * mask).sum() / (mask.sum() + 1e-8)\n\n\ndef smoothness_loss(pred, target):\n    pred_diff = pred[:, 1:] - pred[:, :-1]\n    target_diff = target[:, 1:] - target[:, :-1]\n    return torch.mean(torch.abs(pred_diff - target_diff))\n\n\ndef rr_difference_loss(pred, target, mask):\n    \"\"\"\n    RR difference dynamics loss near missing points.\n    This teaches the model the change pattern of RR intervals.\n    \"\"\"\n    missing = 1.0 - mask\n    pred_diff = pred[:, 1:] - pred[:, :-1]\n    target_diff = target[:, 1:] - target[:, :-1]\n    missing_neighbor = torch.clamp(missing[:, 1:] + missing[:, :-1], 0.0, 1.0)\n    return (torch.abs(pred_diff - target_diff) * missing_neighbor).sum() / (missing_neighbor.sum() + 1e-8)\n\n\ndef hrv_feature_loss(pred, target):\n    pred_feat = differentiable_hrv_features(pred)\n    target_feat = differentiable_hrv_features(target)\n\n    scale = torch.tensor([0.8, 80.0, 150.0, 50.0, 10.0], dtype=torch.float32, device=pred.device)\n    weights = torch.tensor([1.0, 1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 3.0], dtype=torch.float32, device=pred.device)\n\n    rel_abs = torch.abs(pred_feat - target_feat) / (scale + 1e-8)\n    return torch.mean(rel_abs * weights)\n\n\ndef hrv_bias_loss(pred, target):\n    pred_feat = differentiable_hrv_features(pred)\n    target_feat = differentiable_hrv_features(target)\n    diff = pred_feat - target_feat\n\n    scale = torch.tensor([0.8, 80.0, 150.0, 50.0, 10.0], dtype=torch.float32, device=pred.device)\n    weights = torch.tensor([1.0, 1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 3.0], dtype=torch.float32, device=pred.device)\n\n    batch_bias = torch.mean(diff, dim=0)\n    return torch.mean(torch.abs(batch_bias) / (scale + 1e-8) * weights)\n\n\ndef signed_error_balance_loss(pred, target, mask):\n    missing = 1.0 - mask\n    signed_error = (pred - target) * missing\n    return torch.abs(signed_error.sum() / (missing.sum() + 1e-8))\n\n\ndef total_slrdi_bhc_loss(final_pred, slrdi_filled, target, mask):\n    \"\"\"\n    Full training loss.\n\n    final_pred:\n        output after SLRDI + BHC-MAHPI refinement\n    slrdi_filled:\n        initial self-learned interpolation output\n    target:\n        true complete RR\n    mask:\n        1 observed, 0 missing\n    \"\"\"\n    # Final model losses\n    l_mae = masked_mae_loss(final_pred, target, mask)\n    l_mse = masked_mse_loss(final_pred, target, mask)\n    l_diff = rr_difference_loss(final_pred, target, mask)\n    l_hrv = hrv_feature_loss(final_pred, target)\n    l_bias = hrv_bias_loss(final_pred, target)\n    l_smooth = smoothness_loss(final_pred, target)\n    l_cons = observed_consistency_loss(final_pred, target, mask)\n    l_signed = signed_error_balance_loss(final_pred, target, mask)\n    l_huber = masked_huber_loss(final_pred, target, mask, delta=HUBER_DELTA_NORM)\n    l_outlier = outlier_penalty_loss(final_pred, target, mask, threshold_ms=OUTLIER_ERROR_THRESHOLD_MS)\n\n    # Self-learning interpolation should also be close to target at missing positions.\n    l_slrdi_mae = masked_mae_loss(slrdi_filled, target, mask)\n    l_slrdi_diff = rr_difference_loss(slrdi_filled, target, mask)\n\n    loss = (\n        1.00 * l_mae\n        + 0.35 * l_mse\n        + 0.45 * l_diff\n        + 0.80 * l_hrv\n        + 1.00 * l_bias\n        + 0.10 * l_smooth\n        + 0.10 * l_cons\n        + 0.30 * l_signed\n        + 0.40 * l_slrdi_mae\n        + 0.25 * l_slrdi_diff\n        + HUBER_LOSS_WEIGHT * l_huber\n        + OUTLIER_LOSS_WEIGHT * l_outlier\n    )\n\n    parts = {\n        \"mae\": l_mae.item(),\n        \"mse\": l_mse.item(),\n        \"diff\": l_diff.item(),\n        \"hrv\": l_hrv.item(),\n        \"bias\": l_bias.item(),\n        \"smooth\": l_smooth.item(),\n        \"cons\": l_cons.item(),\n        \"signed\": l_signed.item(),\n        \"huber\": l_huber.item(),\n        \"outlier\": l_outlier.item(),\n        \"slrdi_mae\": l_slrdi_mae.item(),\n        \"slrdi_diff\": l_slrdi_diff.item()\n    }\n\n    return loss, parts\n\n\ndef slrdi_pretrain_loss(slrdi_filled, target, mask):\n    l_mae = masked_mae_loss(slrdi_filled, target, mask)\n    l_mse = masked_mse_loss(slrdi_filled, target, mask)\n    l_diff = rr_difference_loss(slrdi_filled, target, mask)\n    l_smooth = smoothness_loss(slrdi_filled, target)\n    l_huber = masked_huber_loss(slrdi_filled, target, mask, delta=HUBER_DELTA_NORM)\n    l_outlier = outlier_penalty_loss(slrdi_filled, target, mask, threshold_ms=OUTLIER_ERROR_THRESHOLD_MS)\n\n    loss = 1.0 * l_mae + 0.4 * l_mse + 0.6 * l_diff + 0.05 * l_smooth + 0.2 * l_huber + 0.1 * l_outlier\n\n    return loss\n\n# ============================================================\n# 12. TRAINING AND EVALUATION\n# ============================================================\n\ndef pretrain_slrdi_one_epoch(model, loader, optimizer):\n    model.train()\n    epoch_loss = 0.0\n\n    for x, y, mask in tqdm(loader, desc=\"Pretraining SLRDI\", leave=False):\n        x = x.to(DEVICE)\n        y = y.to(DEVICE)\n        mask = mask.to(DEVICE)\n\n        optimizer.zero_grad()\n\n        _, slrdi_filled, _ = model(x, return_intermediate=True)\n        loss = slrdi_pretrain_loss(slrdi_filled, y, mask)\n\n        loss.backward()\n        torch.nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(model.parameters(), max_norm=1.0)\n        optimizer.step()\n\n        epoch_loss += loss.item()\n\n    return epoch_loss / len(loader)\n\n\ndef train_one_epoch(model, loader, optimizer):\n    model.train()\n    epoch_loss = 0.0\n    part_sums = None\n    n_batches = 0\n\n    for x, y, mask in tqdm(loader, desc=\"Training\", leave=False):\n        x = x.to(DEVICE)\n        y = y.to(DEVICE)\n        mask = mask.to(DEVICE)\n\n        optimizer.zero_grad()\n\n        final_pred, slrdi_filled, _ = model(x, return_intermediate=True)\n        loss, parts = total_slrdi_bhc_loss(final_pred, slrdi_filled, y, mask)\n\n        loss.backward()\n        torch.nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(model.parameters(), max_norm=1.0)\n        optimizer.step()\n\n        epoch_loss += loss.item()\n\n        if part_sums is None:\n            part_sums = {k: 0.0 for k in parts.keys()}\n\n        for k, v in parts.items():\n            part_sums[k] += v\n\n        n_batches += 1\n\n    avg_parts = {k: v / max(n_batches, 1) for k, v in part_sums.items()}\n\n    return epoch_loss / len(loader), avg_parts\n\n\ndef evaluate_missing_prediction(model, loader, rr_mean=None, rr_std=None, apply_clip=True):\n    \"\"\"\n    Evaluates only missing positions.\n\n    Important outlier fix:\n    - Raw predictions are saved.\n    - If apply_clip=True, predictions are clipped to the physiological RR range\n      before seconds/ms metrics are calculated.\n    - Both raw and clipped max-error statistics are reported when rr_mean and rr_std are provided.\n    \"\"\"\n    model.eval()\n    true_missing = []\n    pred_missing_raw = []\n\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        for x, y, mask in tqdm(loader, desc=\"Evaluating\", leave=False):\n            x = x.to(DEVICE)\n            y = y.to(DEVICE)\n            mask = mask.to(DEVICE)\n\n            pred = model(x)\n            missing = mask == 0\n\n            true_missing.extend(y[missing].cpu().numpy())\n            pred_missing_raw.extend(pred[missing].cpu().numpy())\n\n    true_missing = np.array(true_missing, dtype=np.float64)\n    pred_missing_raw = np.array(pred_missing_raw, dtype=np.float64)\n\n    if rr_mean is not None and rr_std is not None and apply_clip:\n        pred_missing_for_norm_metrics = physiological_clip_norm_numpy(\n            pred_missing_raw.astype(np.float32), rr_mean, rr_std\n        ).astype(np.float64)\n    else:\n        pred_missing_for_norm_metrics = pred_missing_raw\n\n    mae_norm = mean_absolute_error(true_missing, pred_missing_for_norm_metrics)\n    mse_norm = mean_squared_error(true_missing, pred_missing_for_norm_metrics)\n    rmse_norm = np.sqrt(mse_norm)\n    r2_norm = r2_score(true_missing, pred_missing_for_norm_metrics)\n\n    abs_error_norm = np.abs(pred_missing_for_norm_metrics - true_missing)\n\n    metrics = {\n        \"N_missing_points\": int(len(true_missing)),\n        \"Eval_Physiological_Clipping_Applied\": bool(apply_clip and rr_mean is not None and rr_std is not None),\n        \"MAE_norm\": float(mae_norm),\n        \"MSE_norm\": float(mse_norm),\n        \"RMSE_norm\": float(rmse_norm),\n        \"R2_norm\": float(r2_norm),\n        \"MedianAE_norm\": float(np.median(abs_error_norm)),\n        \"P90AE_norm\": float(np.percentile(abs_error_norm, 90)),\n        \"P95AE_norm\": float(np.percentile(abs_error_norm, 95)),\n        \"P99AE_norm\": float(np.percentile(abs_error_norm, 99)),\n        \"MaxAE_norm\": float(np.max(abs_error_norm)),\n    }\n\n    if rr_mean is not None and rr_std is not None:\n        true_seconds = true_missing * rr_std + rr_mean\n        true_seconds = np.clip(true_seconds, PHYS_RR_MIN_SEC, PHYS_RR_MAX_SEC)\n\n        pred_seconds_raw = pred_missing_raw * rr_std + rr_mean\n        pred_seconds_clipped = np.clip(pred_seconds_raw, PHYS_RR_MIN_SEC, PHYS_RR_MAX_SEC)\n        pred_seconds = pred_seconds_clipped if apply_clip else pred_seconds_raw\n\n        raw_error_seconds = pred_seconds_raw - true_seconds\n        clipped_error_seconds = pred_seconds_clipped - true_seconds\n\n        error_seconds = pred_seconds - true_seconds\n        abs_error_seconds = np.abs(error_seconds)\n\n        true_ms = true_seconds * 1000.0\n        pred_ms = pred_seconds * 1000.0\n        error_ms = error_seconds * 1000.0\n        abs_error_ms = abs_error_seconds * 1000.0\n\n        raw_abs_error_ms = np.abs(raw_error_seconds) * 1000.0\n        clipped_abs_error_ms = np.abs(clipped_error_seconds) * 1000.0\n\n        mae_seconds = mean_absolute_error(true_seconds, pred_seconds)\n        mse_seconds2 = mean_squared_error(true_seconds, pred_seconds)\n        rmse_seconds = np.sqrt(mse_seconds2)\n\n        mae_ms = mean_absolute_error(true_ms, pred_ms)\n        mse_ms2 = mean_squared_error(true_ms, pred_ms)\n        rmse_ms = np.sqrt(mse_ms2)\n\n        relative_error_percent = (abs_error_seconds / (np.abs(true_seconds) + 1e-8)) * 100.0\n        signed_relative_error_percent = (error_seconds / (np.abs(true_seconds) + 1e-8)) * 100.0\n\n        metrics.update({\n            \"RR_mean_seconds\": float(rr_mean),\n            \"RR_std_seconds\": float(rr_std),\n            \"RR_std_ms\": float(rr_std * 1000.0),\n            \"Phys_RR_Min_seconds\": float(PHYS_RR_MIN_SEC),\n            \"Phys_RR_Max_seconds\": float(PHYS_RR_MAX_SEC),\n\n            \"MAE_seconds\": float(mae_seconds),\n            \"MSE_seconds2\": float(mse_seconds2),\n            \"RMSE_seconds\": float(rmse_seconds),\n\n            \"MAE_ms\": float(mae_ms),\n            \"MSE_ms2\": float(mse_ms2),\n            \"RMSE_ms\": float(rmse_ms),\n\n            \"Mean_Error_ms\": float(np.mean(error_ms)),\n            \"MedianAE_ms\": float(np.median(abs_error_ms)),\n            \"P90AE_ms\": float(np.percentile(abs_error_ms, 90)),\n            \"P95AE_ms\": float(np.percentile(abs_error_ms, 95)),\n            \"P99AE_ms\": float(np.percentile(abs_error_ms, 99)),\n            \"MaxAE_ms\": float(np.max(abs_error_ms)),\n\n            \"Raw_MaxAE_ms_before_clip\": float(np.max(raw_abs_error_ms)),\n            \"Clipped_MaxAE_ms\": float(np.max(clipped_abs_error_ms)),\n            \"Raw_N_error_gt_100ms\": int(np.sum(raw_abs_error_ms > 100.0)),\n            \"Raw_N_error_gt_200ms\": int(np.sum(raw_abs_error_ms > 200.0)),\n            \"Raw_N_error_gt_500ms\": int(np.sum(raw_abs_error_ms > 500.0)),\n            \"Clipped_N_error_gt_100ms\": int(np.sum(clipped_abs_error_ms > 100.0)),\n            \"Clipped_N_error_gt_200ms\": int(np.sum(clipped_abs_error_ms > 200.0)),\n            \"Clipped_N_error_gt_500ms\": int(np.sum(clipped_abs_error_ms > 500.0)),\n            \"Raw_Percent_error_gt_100ms\": float(100.0 * np.mean(raw_abs_error_ms > 100.0)),\n            \"Clipped_Percent_error_gt_100ms\": float(100.0 * np.mean(clipped_abs_error_ms > 100.0)),\n\n            \"Mean_Relative_Error_percent\": float(np.mean(relative_error_percent)),\n            \"Median_Relative_Error_percent\": float(np.median(relative_error_percent)),\n            \"P90_Relative_Error_percent\": float(np.percentile(relative_error_percent, 90)),\n            \"P95_Relative_Error_percent\": float(np.percentile(relative_error_percent, 95)),\n            \"P99_Relative_Error_percent\": float(np.percentile(relative_error_percent, 99)),\n            \"Max_Relative_Error_percent\": float(np.max(relative_error_percent)),\n\n            \"MAPE_percent\": float(np.mean(relative_error_percent)),\n            \"Signed_Mean_Relative_Error_percent\": float(np.mean(signed_relative_error_percent)),\n        })\n\n    return metrics\n\n\ndef collect_missing_point_errors(model, dataset, rr_mean, rr_std, device=\"cuda\", apply_clip=True):\n    \"\"\"\n    Saves detailed information for every missing RR prediction.\n    This is the main tool for finding outlier source windows and records.\n    \"\"\"\n    model.eval()\n    rows = []\n\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        for window_idx in tqdm(range(len(dataset)), desc=\"Collecting missing-point errors\"):\n            x, y, mask = dataset[window_idx]\n\n            pred = model(x.unsqueeze(0).to(device)).cpu().squeeze(0).numpy()\n            y_np = y.numpy()\n            mask_np = mask.numpy()\n            corrupted_np = x[0].numpy()\n\n            if apply_clip:\n                pred_eval = physiological_clip_norm_numpy(pred, rr_mean, rr_std)\n            else:\n                pred_eval = pred\n\n            missing_indices = np.where(mask_np == 0)[0]\n            record_name = None\n            if getattr(dataset, \"window_record_ids\", None) is not None:\n                record_name = dataset.window_record_ids[window_idx]\n\n            for pos in missing_indices:\n                true_norm = y_np[pos]\n                pred_norm_raw = pred[pos]\n                pred_norm_eval = pred_eval[pos]\n\n                true_sec = true_norm * rr_std + rr_mean\n                pred_sec_raw = pred_norm_raw * rr_std + rr_mean\n                pred_sec_eval = pred_norm_eval * rr_std + rr_mean\n\n                raw_error_ms = (pred_sec_raw - true_sec) * 1000.0\n                eval_error_ms = (pred_sec_eval - true_sec) * 1000.0\n\n                left = max(0, pos - 5)\n                right = min(len(y_np), pos + 6)\n                local_true_sec = y_np[left:right] * rr_std + rr_mean\n                local_range_ms = (np.max(local_true_sec) - np.min(local_true_sec)) * 1000.0\n\n                rows.append({\n                    \"record\": record_name,\n                    \"window_idx\": int(window_idx),\n                    \"position_in_window\": int(pos),\n                    \"is_edge_position\": bool(pos < 10 or pos > WINDOW_SIZE - 10),\n                    \"true_norm\": float(true_norm),\n                    \"pred_norm_raw\": float(pred_norm_raw),\n                    \"pred_norm_eval\": float(pred_norm_eval),\n                    \"corrupted_norm\": float(corrupted_np[pos]),\n                    \"true_sec\": float(true_sec),\n                    \"pred_sec_raw\": float(pred_sec_raw),\n                    \"pred_sec_eval\": float(pred_sec_eval),\n                    \"true_ms\": float(true_sec * 1000.0),\n                    \"pred_ms_raw\": float(pred_sec_raw * 1000.0),\n                    \"pred_ms_eval\": float(pred_sec_eval * 1000.0),\n                    \"raw_error_ms\": float(raw_error_ms),\n                    \"raw_abs_error_ms\": float(abs(raw_error_ms)),\n                    \"eval_error_ms\": float(eval_error_ms),\n                    \"eval_abs_error_ms\": float(abs(eval_error_ms)),\n                    \"local_true_range_ms_radius5\": float(local_range_ms),\n                    \"raw_pred_below_phys_min\": bool(pred_sec_raw < PHYS_RR_MIN_SEC),\n                    \"raw_pred_above_phys_max\": bool(pred_sec_raw > PHYS_RR_MAX_SEC),\n                })\n\n    df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    df = df.sort_values(\"eval_abs_error_ms\", ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n    return df\n\n\ndef summarize_outliers(outlier_df, threshold_ms=OUTLIER_ERROR_THRESHOLD_MS):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a compact summary of outlier counts and likely causes.\n\n    This fixed version works for both:\n        1. Old window-level outlier table:\n           is_edge_position, position_in_window\n        2. New paper-style full-sequence outlier table:\n           position_in_full_sequence\n\n    It prevents KeyError when the full-sequence outlier table does not contain\n    is_edge_position.\n    \"\"\"\n    total = len(outlier_df)\n\n    if total == 0:\n        print(\"\\nNo outliers found because outlier_df is empty.\")\n        return pd.DataFrame()\n\n    df = outlier_df.copy()\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Make this function robust for both old and new outlier tables.\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------\n    if \"is_edge_position\" not in df.columns:\n        df[\"is_edge_position\"] = False\n\n    if \"raw_pred_below_phys_min\" not in df.columns:\n        df[\"raw_pred_below_phys_min\"] = False\n\n    if \"raw_pred_above_phys_max\" not in df.columns:\n        df[\"raw_pred_above_phys_max\"] = False\n\n    if \"raw_abs_error_ms\" not in df.columns and \"eval_abs_error_ms\" in df.columns:\n        df[\"raw_abs_error_ms\"] = df[\"eval_abs_error_ms\"]\n\n    if \"eval_abs_error_ms\" not in df.columns and \"raw_abs_error_ms\" in df.columns:\n        df[\"eval_abs_error_ms\"] = df[\"raw_abs_error_ms\"]\n\n    if \"record\" not in df.columns:\n        df[\"record\"] = \"unknown\"\n\n    rows = []\n\n    for thr in [50.0, 100.0, 200.0, 500.0, 1000.0]:\n        rows.append({\n            \"threshold_ms\": thr,\n            \"raw_count\": int((df[\"raw_abs_error_ms\"] > thr).sum()),\n            \"raw_percent\": float(100.0 * (df[\"raw_abs_error_ms\"] > thr).mean()),\n            \"eval_count\": int((df[\"eval_abs_error_ms\"] > thr).sum()),\n            \"eval_percent\": float(100.0 * (df[\"eval_abs_error_ms\"] > thr).mean()),\n        })\n\n    summary = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n\n    print(\"\\nOutlier count summary:\")\n    display(summary)\n\n    print(\"\\nTop likely cause counts among evaluated outliers:\")\n\n    severe = df[df[\"eval_abs_error_ms\"] > threshold_ms]\n\n    print(\"Total severe evaluated outliers:\", len(severe))\n\n    if len(severe) > 0:\n        print(\"Edge-position severe outliers:\", int(severe[\"is_edge_position\"].sum()))\n        print(\"Raw predictions below physiological min:\", int(severe[\"raw_pred_below_phys_min\"].sum()))\n        print(\"Raw predictions above physiological max:\", int(severe[\"raw_pred_above_phys_max\"].sum()))\n\n        print(\"Records with most severe outliers:\")\n        display(severe[\"record\"].value_counts().head(10))\n\n    return summary\n\ndef visualize_outlier_window(model, dataset, outlier_df, rank=0, device=\"cuda\", apply_clip=True):\n    \"\"\"Visualize one outlier window. rank=0 means largest evaluated absolute error.\"\"\"\n    row = outlier_df.iloc[rank]\n    window_idx = int(row[\"window_idx\"])\n    bad_pos = int(row[\"position_in_window\"])\n\n    model.eval()\n    x, y, mask = dataset[window_idx]\n\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        pred, slrdi_filled, _ = model(\n            x.unsqueeze(0).to(device),\n            return_intermediate=True\n        )\n        pred = pred.cpu().squeeze(0).numpy()\n        slrdi_filled = slrdi_filled.cpu().squeeze(0).numpy()\n\n    if apply_clip:\n        pred_plot = physiological_clip_norm_numpy(pred, rr_mean, rr_std)\n    else:\n        pred_plot = pred\n\n    y_np = y.numpy()\n    mask_np = mask.numpy()\n    corrupted_np = x[0].numpy()\n    missing_idx = np.where(mask_np == 0)[0]\n\n    plt.figure(figsize=(16, 5))\n    plt.plot(y_np, label=\"True normalized RR\", linewidth=2)\n    plt.plot(corrupted_np, label=\"Corrupted RR input\", linewidth=1)\n    plt.plot(slrdi_filled, label=\"SLRDI interpolation\", linestyle=\"--\")\n    plt.plot(pred_plot, label=\"Final prediction used for evaluation\", linestyle=\"-.\")\n\n    plt.scatter(missing_idx, y_np[missing_idx], label=\"True missing RR\", marker=\"o\")\n    plt.scatter(missing_idx, pred_plot[missing_idx], label=\"Predicted missing RR\", marker=\"x\")\n    plt.axvline(bad_pos, linestyle=\":\", linewidth=2, label=f\"Outlier position {bad_pos}\")\n\n    title_record = row[\"record\"] if pd.notna(row[\"record\"]) else \"unknown record\"\n    plt.title(\n        f\"Outlier rank {rank} | Record {title_record} | Window {window_idx} | \"\n        f\"Position {bad_pos} | Error {row['eval_abs_error_ms']:.2f} ms\"\n    )\n    plt.xlabel(\"Position in window\")\n    plt.ylabel(\"Normalized RR\")\n    plt.legend()\n    plt.grid(True)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.show()\n\n\ndef print_outlier_context(dataset, outlier_df, rank=0, radius=10):\n    \"\"\"Print neighboring true RR values around an outlier.\"\"\"\n    row = outlier_df.iloc[rank]\n    window_idx = int(row[\"window_idx\"])\n    pos = int(row[\"position_in_window\"])\n\n    x, y, mask = dataset[window_idx]\n    y_np = y.numpy()\n    mask_np = mask.numpy()\n\n    left = max(0, pos - radius)\n    right = min(len(y_np), pos + radius + 1)\n\n    context = pd.DataFrame({\n        \"position\": np.arange(left, right),\n        \"true_norm\": y_np[left:right],\n        \"mask_1_observed_0_missing\": mask_np[left:right]\n    })\n    context[\"true_sec\"] = context[\"true_norm\"] * rr_std + rr_mean\n    context[\"true_ms\"] = context[\"true_sec\"] * 1000.0\n    context[\"is_outlier_position\"] = context[\"position\"] == pos\n\n    display(context)\n    return context\n\n# ============================================================\n# 13. TRAIN MODEL\n# ============================================================\n\nmodel = SLRDI_BHC_MAHPINet(\n    seq_len=WINDOW_SIZE,\n    d_model=64,\n    nhead=4,\n    num_transformer_layers=2,\n    lstm_hidden=64,\n    dropout=0.1\n).to(DEVICE)\n\noptimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=LR, weight_decay=WEIGHT_DECAY)\nscheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.ReduceLROnPlateau(\n    optimizer,\n    mode=\"min\",\n    factor=0.5,\n    patience=7,\n    min_lr=1e-6\n)\n\ntotal_params = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters())\ntrainable_params = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters() if p.requires_grad)\n\nprint(\"\\nModel initialized.\")\nprint(\"Total parameters:\", total_params)\nprint(\"Trainable parameters:\", trainable_params)\n\nbest_val_rmse = float(\"inf\")\nbest_model_path = RESULTS_DIR / \"best_slrdi_bhc_mahpi_net.pt\"\nhistory = []\n\nif USE_SLRDI_PRETRAIN:\n    print(\"\\nPretraining self-learning RR-difference interpolation module...\")\n    for epoch in range(1, SLRDI_PRETRAIN_EPOCHS + 1):\n        pretrain_loss = pretrain_slrdi_one_epoch(model, train_loader, optimizer)\n        val_metrics = evaluate_missing_prediction(model, val_loader, rr_mean=rr_mean, rr_std=rr_std)\n        print(\n            f\"SLRDI Pretrain Epoch {epoch:03d} | \"\n            f\"Loss: {pretrain_loss:.6f} | \"\n            f\"Val MAE_ms: {val_metrics['MAE_ms']:.3f} | \"\n            f\"Val RMSE_ms: {val_metrics['RMSE_ms']:.3f} | \"\n            f\"Val R2: {val_metrics['R2_norm']:.4f}\"\n        )\n\nprint(\"\\nTraining full SLRDI-BHC-MAHPI-Net...\")\n\nfor epoch in range(1, EPOCHS + 1):\n    train_loss, train_parts = train_one_epoch(model, train_loader, optimizer)\n\n    val_metrics = evaluate_missing_prediction(model, val_loader, rr_mean=rr_mean, rr_std=rr_std)\n    scheduler.step(val_metrics[\"RMSE_norm\"])\n    current_lr = optimizer.param_groups[0][\"lr\"]\n\n    print(\n        f\"Epoch {epoch:03d} | \"\n        f\"LR: {current_lr:.2e} | \"\n        f\"Train Loss: {train_loss:.6f} | \"\n        f\"Val MAE_norm: {val_metrics['MAE_norm']:.6f} | \"\n        f\"Val RMSE_norm: {val_metrics['RMSE_norm']:.6f} | \"\n        f\"Val R2: {val_metrics['R2_norm']:.4f} | \"\n        f\"Val MAE_ms: {val_metrics['MAE_ms']:.3f} | \"\n        f\"Val RMSE_ms: {val_metrics['RMSE_ms']:.3f} | \"\n        f\"Val MAPE: {val_metrics['MAPE_percent']:.3f}%\"\n    )\n\n    row = {\n        \"epoch\": epoch,\n        \"learning_rate\": current_lr,\n        \"train_loss\": train_loss\n    }\n    row.update(val_metrics)\n    for k, v in train_parts.items():\n        row[f\"train_{k}\"] = v\n    history.append(row)\n\n    if val_metrics[\"RMSE_norm\"] < best_val_rmse:\n        best_val_rmse = val_metrics[\"RMSE_norm\"]\n        torch.save(model.state_dict(), best_model_path)\n        print(\"Best model saved.\")\n\nhistory_df = pd.DataFrame(history)\nhistory_path = RESULTS_DIR / \"training_history_slrdi_bhc_mahpi.csv\"\nhistory_df.to_csv(history_path, index=False)\n\nprint(\"\\nTraining complete.\")\nprint(\"Best model:\", best_model_path)\n\n# ============================================================\n# 14. TRAINING CURVES\n# ============================================================\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\nplt.plot(history_df[\"epoch\"], history_df[\"train_loss\"], label=\"Train Loss\")\nplt.xlabel(\"Epoch\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Loss\")\nplt.title(\"Training Loss - SLRDI-BHC-MAHPI-Net\")\nplt.legend()\nplt.grid(True)\nplt.show()\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\nplt.plot(history_df[\"epoch\"], history_df[\"RMSE_norm\"], label=\"Validation RMSE norm\")\nplt.xlabel(\"Epoch\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Normalized RMSE\")\nplt.title(\"Validation RMSE Norm\")\nplt.legend()\nplt.grid(True)\nplt.show()\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\nplt.plot(history_df[\"epoch\"], history_df[\"RMSE_ms\"], label=\"Validation RMSE ms\")\nplt.xlabel(\"Epoch\")\nplt.ylabel(\"RMSE ms\")\nplt.title(\"Validation RMSE in Milliseconds\")\nplt.legend()\nplt.grid(True)\nplt.show()\n\n# ============================================================\n# 15. HRV FUNCTIONS\n# ============================================================\n\ndef compute_time_domain_hrv(rr_seconds):\n    rr_seconds = np.asarray(rr_seconds, dtype=np.float64)\n    rr_seconds = rr_seconds[np.isfinite(rr_seconds)]\n    rr_seconds = rr_seconds[(rr_seconds > PHYS_RR_MIN_SEC) & (rr_seconds < PHYS_RR_MAX_SEC)]\n\n    if len(rr_seconds) < 3:\n        return {\n            \"meanNN (s)\": np.nan,\n            \"HR (bpm)\": np.nan,\n            \"SDNN (ms)\": np.nan,\n            \"RMSSD (ms)\": np.nan,\n            \"pNN50 (%)\": np.nan\n        }\n\n    rr_ms = rr_seconds * 1000.0\n    mean_nn = np.mean(rr_seconds)\n    hr = 60.0 / mean_nn\n    sdnn = np.std(rr_ms, ddof=1)\n    diff_rr_ms = np.diff(rr_ms)\n    rmssd = np.sqrt(np.mean(diff_rr_ms ** 2))\n    nn50 = np.sum(np.abs(diff_rr_ms) > 50.0)\n    pnn50 = 100.0 * nn50 / len(diff_rr_ms)\n\n    return {\n        \"meanNN (s)\": mean_nn,\n        \"HR (bpm)\": hr,\n        \"SDNN (ms)\": sdnn,\n        \"RMSSD (ms)\": rmssd,\n        \"pNN50 (%)\": pnn50\n    }\n\n\ndef compute_frequency_domain_hrv(rr_seconds, fs_interp=4.0):\n    rr_seconds = np.asarray(rr_seconds, dtype=np.float64)\n    rr_seconds = rr_seconds[np.isfinite(rr_seconds)]\n    rr_seconds = rr_seconds[(rr_seconds > PHYS_RR_MIN_SEC) & (rr_seconds < PHYS_RR_MAX_SEC)]\n\n    if len(rr_seconds) < 20:\n        return {\"VLF (%)\": np.nan, \"LF (%)\": np.nan, \"HF (%)\": np.nan, \"LF/HF\": np.nan}\n\n    time_rr = np.cumsum(rr_seconds)\n    time_rr = time_rr - time_rr[0]\n\n    if time_rr[-1] <= 10:\n        return {\"VLF (%)\": np.nan, \"LF (%)\": np.nan, \"HF (%)\": np.nan, \"LF/HF\": np.nan}\n\n    t_interp = np.arange(0, time_rr[-1], 1.0 / fs_interp)\n    if len(t_interp) < 20:\n        return {\"VLF (%)\": np.nan, \"LF (%)\": np.nan, \"HF (%)\": np.nan, \"LF/HF\": np.nan}\n\n    try:\n        rr_interp = np.interp(t_interp, time_rr, rr_seconds)\n        rr_interp = rr_interp - np.mean(rr_interp)\n        nperseg = min(256, len(rr_interp))\n        freqs, psd = signal.welch(rr_interp, fs=fs_interp, nperseg=nperseg)\n\n        def band_power(low, high):\n            idx = (freqs >= low) & (freqs < high)\n            if np.sum(idx) < 1:\n                return 0.0\n            return np.trapz(psd[idx], freqs[idx])\n\n        vlf_power = band_power(0.0033, 0.04)\n        lf_power = band_power(0.04, 0.15)\n        hf_power = band_power(0.15, 0.40)\n        total_power = vlf_power + lf_power + hf_power\n\n        if total_power <= 0:\n            return {\"VLF (%)\": np.nan, \"LF (%)\": np.nan, \"HF (%)\": np.nan, \"LF/HF\": np.nan}\n\n        return {\n            \"VLF (%)\": 100.0 * vlf_power / total_power,\n            \"LF (%)\": 100.0 * lf_power / total_power,\n            \"HF (%)\": 100.0 * hf_power / total_power,\n            \"LF/HF\": lf_power / hf_power if hf_power > 0 else np.nan\n        }\n\n    except Exception:\n        return {\"VLF (%)\": np.nan, \"LF (%)\": np.nan, \"HF (%)\": np.nan, \"LF/HF\": np.nan}\n\n\ndef compute_all_hrv(rr_seconds):\n    hrv = {}\n    hrv.update(compute_time_domain_hrv(rr_seconds))\n    hrv.update(compute_frequency_domain_hrv(rr_seconds))\n    return hrv\n\n# ============================================================\n# 16. FULL-SEQUENCE IMPUTATION\n# ============================================================\n\ndef make_full_sequence_features(corrupted, mask):\n    diff = rr_difference_feature(corrupted)\n    slope = rr_local_slope_feature(corrupted)\n    local_mean = rr_local_mean_feature(corrupted, window=9)\n    return np.stack([corrupted, mask, diff, slope, local_mean], axis=0).astype(np.float32)\n\n\ndef impute_one_sequence_with_model(\n    model,\n    rr_sequence_seconds,\n    rr_mean,\n    rr_std,\n    missing_rate=0.05,\n    missing_type=\"random\",\n    window_size=256,\n    stride=128,\n    device=\"cuda\"\n):\n    model.eval()\n\n    rr = np.asarray(rr_sequence_seconds, dtype=np.float32)\n    rr = rr[np.isfinite(rr)]\n    rr = rr[(rr > PHYS_RR_MIN_SEC) & (rr < PHYS_RR_MAX_SEC)]\n\n    if len(rr) < window_size:\n        return None, None, None\n\n    rr_norm = (rr - rr_mean) / (rr_std + 1e-8)\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Missing-value creation\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------\n    # For final comparison with the paper, use the paper-style real-time\n    # 5-min window / 4-min overlap / 1-min step deletion procedure.\n    # The model itself still imputes using its trained 256-RR windows.\n    if missing_type in [\"paper_realtime_5min\", \"realtime_5min\"]:\n        full_mask = apply_paper_realtime_5min_missing_mask(\n            rr_seconds=rr,\n            missing_rate=missing_rate,\n            window_sec=300.0,\n            step_sec=60.0,\n            edge_margin_beats=2,\n            seed=None\n        )\n        corrupted = rr_norm.copy()\n        corrupted[full_mask == 0.0] = 0.0\n    else:\n        corrupted, full_mask = apply_missing(\n            rr_norm,\n            missing_rate=missing_rate,\n            missing_type=missing_type\n        )\n\n    pred_sum = np.zeros_like(rr_norm, dtype=np.float32)\n    pred_count = np.zeros_like(rr_norm, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    starts = list(range(0, len(rr_norm) - window_size + 1, stride))\n    if starts[-1] != len(rr_norm) - window_size:\n        starts.append(len(rr_norm) - window_size)\n\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        for start in starts:\n            end = start + window_size\n            x_window = corrupted[start:end]\n            m_window = full_mask[start:end]\n            x_input = make_full_sequence_features(x_window, m_window)\n            x_input = torch.tensor(x_input, dtype=torch.float32).unsqueeze(0).to(device)\n            pred_window = model(x_input).cpu().numpy().squeeze(0)\n            pred_sum[start:end] += pred_window\n            pred_count[start:end] += 1.0\n\n    pred_norm = pred_sum / np.maximum(pred_count, 1e-8)\n\n    imputed_norm = rr_norm.copy()\n    imputed_norm[full_mask == 0] = pred_norm[full_mask == 0]\n\n    imputed_rr = imputed_norm * rr_std + rr_mean\n    imputed_rr = np.clip(imputed_rr, PHYS_RR_MIN_SEC, PHYS_RR_MAX_SEC)\n\n    return rr, imputed_rr, full_mask\n\n\ndef evaluate_full_sequence_missing_prediction(\n    model,\n    all_rr_subset,\n    rr_mean,\n    rr_std,\n    missing_rate=0.10,\n    missing_type=\"paper_realtime_5min\",\n    repeats=1,\n    window_size=256,\n    stride=128,\n    device=\"cuda\",\n    apply_clip=True\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Pointwise evaluation for full-sequence missingness.\n\n    This is the correct pointwise evaluation when using the paper-style\n    missing-value procedure, because missing values are created on the full\n    RR sequence using 5-min windows with 4-min overlap.\n\n    Returns:\n        metrics_df row as dict-compatible metrics\n        outlier_df with one row per missing RR interval\n    \"\"\"\n    rows = []\n\n    for record_name, rr_sequence in tqdm(all_rr_subset.items(), desc=\"Full-sequence pointwise evaluation\"):\n        for rep in range(repeats):\n            true_rr, imp_rr, full_mask = impute_one_sequence_with_model(\n                model=model,\n                rr_sequence_seconds=rr_sequence,\n                rr_mean=rr_mean,\n                rr_std=rr_std,\n                missing_rate=missing_rate,\n                missing_type=missing_type,\n                window_size=window_size,\n                stride=stride,\n                device=device\n            )\n\n            if true_rr is None:\n                continue\n\n            missing_idx = np.where(full_mask == 0.0)[0]\n\n            for pos in missing_idx:\n                true_sec = float(true_rr[pos])\n                pred_sec = float(imp_rr[pos])\n\n                if apply_clip:\n                    pred_sec_eval = float(np.clip(pred_sec, PHYS_RR_MIN_SEC, PHYS_RR_MAX_SEC))\n                else:\n                    pred_sec_eval = pred_sec\n\n                error_ms = (pred_sec_eval - true_sec) * 1000.0\n                raw_error_ms = (pred_sec - true_sec) * 1000.0\n\n                left = max(0, pos - 5)\n                right = min(len(true_rr), pos + 6)\n                local_range_ms = float((np.max(true_rr[left:right]) - np.min(true_rr[left:right])) * 1000.0)\n\n                # Full-sequence edge flag:\n                # True only when the missing point is near the start or end of\n                # the complete RR sequence. This column is needed by\n                # summarize_outliers().\n                is_edge_position = bool(\n                    pos < 10 or pos > len(true_rr) - 10\n                )\n\n                rows.append({\n                    \"record\": record_name,\n                    \"repeat\": rep,\n                    \"position_in_full_sequence\": int(pos),\n                    \"is_edge_position\": is_edge_position,\n                    \"true_sec\": true_sec,\n                    \"pred_sec_raw\": pred_sec,\n                    \"pred_sec_eval\": pred_sec_eval,\n                    \"true_ms\": true_sec * 1000.0,\n                    \"pred_ms_raw\": pred_sec * 1000.0,\n                    \"pred_ms_eval\": pred_sec_eval * 1000.0,\n                    \"raw_error_ms\": raw_error_ms,\n                    \"raw_abs_error_ms\": abs(raw_error_ms),\n                    \"eval_error_ms\": error_ms,\n                    \"eval_abs_error_ms\": abs(error_ms),\n                    \"local_true_range_ms_radius5\": local_range_ms,\n                    \"raw_pred_below_phys_min\": bool(pred_sec < PHYS_RR_MIN_SEC),\n                    \"raw_pred_above_phys_max\": bool(pred_sec > PHYS_RR_MAX_SEC),\n                    \"missing_type\": missing_type,\n                    \"missing_rate\": missing_rate,\n                })\n\n    outlier_df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n\n    if len(outlier_df) == 0:\n        return {}, outlier_df\n\n    outlier_df = outlier_df.sort_values(\"eval_abs_error_ms\", ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n\n    true_ms = outlier_df[\"true_ms\"].values\n    pred_ms = outlier_df[\"pred_ms_eval\"].values\n    true_sec = outlier_df[\"true_sec\"].values\n    pred_sec = outlier_df[\"pred_sec_eval\"].values\n\n    error_ms = pred_ms - true_ms\n    abs_error_ms = np.abs(error_ms)\n    rel_error_percent = np.abs(pred_sec - true_sec) / (np.abs(true_sec) + 1e-8) * 100.0\n\n    true_norm = (true_sec - rr_mean) / (rr_std + 1e-8)\n    pred_norm = (pred_sec - rr_mean) / (rr_std + 1e-8)\n\n    metrics = {\n        \"N_missing_points\": int(len(outlier_df)),\n        \"Missing_Type\": missing_type,\n        \"Missing_Rate\": float(missing_rate),\n        \"Eval_Physiological_Clipping_Applied\": bool(apply_clip),\n        \"MAE_norm\": float(mean_absolute_error(true_norm, pred_norm)),\n        \"MSE_norm\": float(mean_squared_error(true_norm, pred_norm)),\n        \"RMSE_norm\": float(np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(true_norm, pred_norm))),\n        \"R2_norm\": float(r2_score(true_norm, pred_norm)),\n        \"MAE_seconds\": float(mean_absolute_error(true_sec, pred_sec)),\n        \"MSE_seconds2\": float(mean_squared_error(true_sec, pred_sec)),\n        \"RMSE_seconds\": float(np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(true_sec, pred_sec))),\n        \"MAE_ms\": float(mean_absolute_error(true_ms, pred_ms)),\n        \"MSE_ms2\": float(mean_squared_error(true_ms, pred_ms)),\n        \"RMSE_ms\": float(np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(true_ms, pred_ms))),\n        \"Mean_Error_ms\": float(np.mean(error_ms)),\n        \"MedianAE_ms\": float(np.median(abs_error_ms)),\n        \"P90AE_ms\": float(np.percentile(abs_error_ms, 90)),\n        \"P95AE_ms\": float(np.percentile(abs_error_ms, 95)),\n        \"P99AE_ms\": float(np.percentile(abs_error_ms, 99)),\n        \"MaxAE_ms\": float(np.max(abs_error_ms)),\n        \"Raw_MaxAE_ms_before_clip\": float(np.max(outlier_df[\"raw_abs_error_ms\"].values)),\n        \"Clipped_MaxAE_ms\": float(np.max(abs_error_ms)),\n        \"Raw_N_error_gt_100ms\": int(np.sum(outlier_df[\"raw_abs_error_ms\"].values > 100.0)),\n        \"Raw_N_error_gt_200ms\": int(np.sum(outlier_df[\"raw_abs_error_ms\"].values > 200.0)),\n        \"Raw_N_error_gt_500ms\": int(np.sum(outlier_df[\"raw_abs_error_ms\"].values > 500.0)),\n        \"Clipped_N_error_gt_100ms\": int(np.sum(abs_error_ms > 100.0)),\n        \"Clipped_N_error_gt_200ms\": int(np.sum(abs_error_ms > 200.0)),\n        \"Clipped_N_error_gt_500ms\": int(np.sum(abs_error_ms > 500.0)),\n        \"Raw_Percent_error_gt_100ms\": float(100.0 * np.mean(outlier_df[\"raw_abs_error_ms\"].values > 100.0)),\n        \"Clipped_Percent_error_gt_100ms\": float(100.0 * np.mean(abs_error_ms > 100.0)),\n        \"Mean_Relative_Error_percent\": float(np.mean(rel_error_percent)),\n        \"Median_Relative_Error_percent\": float(np.median(rel_error_percent)),\n        \"P90_Relative_Error_percent\": float(np.percentile(rel_error_percent, 90)),\n        \"P95_Relative_Error_percent\": float(np.percentile(rel_error_percent, 95)),\n        \"P99_Relative_Error_percent\": float(np.percentile(rel_error_percent, 99)),\n        \"Max_Relative_Error_percent\": float(np.max(rel_error_percent)),\n        \"MAPE_percent\": float(np.mean(rel_error_percent)),\n        \"Signed_Mean_Relative_Error_percent\": float(np.mean((pred_sec - true_sec) / (np.abs(true_sec) + 1e-8) * 100.0)),\n    }\n\n    return metrics, outlier_df\n\n# ============================================================\n# 17. PATIENTWISE HRV TABLES WITH REPEATED MASKS\n# ============================================================\n\ndef compute_patientwise_hrv_tables_repeated(\n    model,\n    all_rr_subset,\n    rr_mean,\n    rr_std,\n    missing_rate=0.05,\n    missing_type=\"random\",\n    repeats=5,\n    window_size=256,\n    stride=128,\n    device=\"cuda\",\n    hrv_calibration_bias=None\n):\n    true_rows = []\n    imp_rows = []\n    error_rows = []\n\n    for record_name, rr_sequence in tqdm(all_rr_subset.items(), desc=\"Patientwise HRV analysis\"):\n        true_hrv_list = []\n        imp_hrv_list = []\n        n_rr = None\n\n        for _ in range(repeats):\n            true_rr, imp_rr, full_mask = impute_one_sequence_with_model(\n                model=model,\n                rr_sequence_seconds=rr_sequence,\n                rr_mean=rr_mean,\n                rr_std=rr_std,\n                missing_rate=missing_rate,\n                missing_type=missing_type,\n                window_size=window_size,\n                stride=stride,\n                device=device\n            )\n\n            if true_rr is None:\n                continue\n\n            n_rr = len(true_rr)\n\n            true_hrv = compute_all_hrv(true_rr)\n            imp_hrv = compute_all_hrv(imp_rr)\n\n            if hrv_calibration_bias is not None:\n                for metric, bias in hrv_calibration_bias.items():\n                    if metric in imp_hrv and np.isfinite(imp_hrv[metric]):\n                        imp_hrv[metric] = imp_hrv[metric] - bias\n\n            true_hrv_list.append(true_hrv)\n            imp_hrv_list.append(imp_hrv)\n\n        if len(true_hrv_list) == 0:\n            continue\n\n        metrics = list(true_hrv_list[0].keys())\n        true_avg = {}\n        imp_avg = {}\n\n        for metric in metrics:\n            true_vals = np.array([d[metric] for d in true_hrv_list], dtype=np.float64)\n            imp_vals = np.array([d[metric] for d in imp_hrv_list], dtype=np.float64)\n            true_avg[metric] = np.nanmean(true_vals)\n            imp_avg[metric] = np.nanmean(imp_vals)\n\n        true_row = {\n            \"Record\": record_name,\n            \"N_RR\": n_rr,\n            \"Missing_Rate\": missing_rate,\n            \"Missing_Type\": missing_type,\n            \"Repeats\": repeats\n        }\n        true_row.update(true_avg)\n\n        imp_row = {\n            \"Record\": record_name,\n            \"N_RR\": n_rr,\n            \"Missing_Rate\": missing_rate,\n            \"Missing_Type\": missing_type,\n            \"Repeats\": repeats\n        }\n        imp_row.update(imp_avg)\n\n        err_row = {\n            \"Record\": record_name,\n            \"N_RR\": n_rr,\n            \"Missing_Rate\": missing_rate,\n            \"Missing_Type\": missing_type,\n            \"Repeats\": repeats\n        }\n\n        for metric in metrics:\n            err_row[f\"{metric}_TRUE\"] = true_avg[metric]\n            err_row[f\"{metric}_IMP\"] = imp_avg[metric]\n            err_row[f\"{metric}_DIFF_IMP_TRUE\"] = imp_avg[metric] - true_avg[metric]\n            err_row[f\"{metric}_ABS_ERROR\"] = abs(imp_avg[metric] - true_avg[metric])\n\n        true_rows.append(true_row)\n        imp_rows.append(imp_row)\n        error_rows.append(err_row)\n\n    return pd.DataFrame(true_rows), pd.DataFrame(imp_rows), pd.DataFrame(error_rows)\n\n# ============================================================\n# 18. VALIDATION-SET HRV CALIBRATION BIAS\n# ============================================================\n\ndef estimate_hrv_calibration_bias(\n    model,\n    val_all_rr,\n    rr_mean,\n    rr_std,\n    missing_rate=0.05,\n    missing_type=\"random\",\n    repeats=3,\n    window_size=256,\n    stride=128,\n    device=\"cuda\"\n):\n    true_df, imp_df, _ = compute_patientwise_hrv_tables_repeated(\n        model=model,\n        all_rr_subset=val_all_rr,\n        rr_mean=rr_mean,\n        rr_std=rr_std,\n        missing_rate=missing_rate,\n        missing_type=missing_type,\n        repeats=repeats,\n        window_size=window_size,\n        stride=stride,\n        device=device,\n        hrv_calibration_bias=None\n    )\n\n    bias = {}\n\n    for metric in HRV_METRICS:\n        if metric in true_df.columns and metric in imp_df.columns:\n            diff = imp_df[metric].values - true_df[metric].values\n            diff = diff[np.isfinite(diff)]\n            bias[metric] = np.mean(diff) if len(diff) > 0 else 0.0\n\n    return bias\n\n# ============================================================\n# 19. T-TEST, TOST, COMBINED SUMMARY\n# ============================================================\n\ndef paired_ttest_true_vs_imputed(true_df, imp_df):\n    rows = []\n\n    for metric in HRV_METRICS:\n        true_values = true_df[metric].values\n        imp_values = imp_df[metric].values\n        valid = np.isfinite(true_values) & np.isfinite(imp_values)\n        true_valid = true_values[valid]\n        imp_valid = imp_values[valid]\n        n = len(true_valid)\n\n        if n < 3:\n            rows.append({\n                \"Metric\": metric,\n                \"N\": n,\n                \"mean_TRUE\": np.nan,\n                \"mean_IMP\": np.nan,\n                \"mean_diff(IMP-TRUE)\": np.nan,\n                \"t_stat\": np.nan,\n                \"p_value\": np.nan\n            })\n            continue\n\n        t_stat, p_value = ttest_rel(imp_valid, true_valid)\n        rows.append({\n            \"Metric\": metric,\n            \"N\": n,\n            \"mean_TRUE\": np.mean(true_valid),\n            \"mean_IMP\": np.mean(imp_valid),\n            \"mean_diff(IMP-TRUE)\": np.mean(imp_valid - true_valid),\n            \"t_stat\": t_stat,\n            \"p_value\": p_value\n        })\n\n    ttest_df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    valid_p = ttest_df[\"p_value\"].notna()\n    q_values = np.full(len(ttest_df), np.nan)\n\n    if valid_p.sum() > 0:\n        _, q_vals, _, _ = multipletests(\n            ttest_df.loc[valid_p, \"p_value\"].values,\n            alpha=0.05,\n            method=\"fdr_bh\"\n        )\n        q_values[valid_p.values] = q_vals\n\n    ttest_df[\"q_value(FDR_BH)\"] = q_values\n    return ttest_df\n\n\ndef tost_paired_equivalence(x_true, x_imp, eq_low, eq_high, alpha=0.05):\n    x_true = np.asarray(x_true, dtype=np.float64)\n    x_imp = np.asarray(x_imp, dtype=np.float64)\n    valid = np.isfinite(x_true) & np.isfinite(x_imp)\n    x_true = x_true[valid]\n    x_imp = x_imp[valid]\n    diff = x_imp - x_true\n    n = len(diff)\n\n    if n < 3:\n        return {\n            \"N\": n,\n            \"mean_diff(IMP-TRUE)\": np.nan,\n            \"p_low\": np.nan,\n            \"p_high\": np.nan,\n            \"p_equivalence\": np.nan,\n            \"Decision (TOST alpha=0.05)\": \"Insufficient data\",\n            \"Interpretation\": \"Insufficient data\"\n        }\n\n    mean_diff = np.mean(diff)\n    sd_diff = np.std(diff, ddof=1)\n    se_diff = sd_diff / np.sqrt(n)\n    df = n - 1\n\n    if se_diff == 0:\n        p_low = 0.0 if mean_diff > eq_low else 1.0\n        p_high = 0.0 if mean_diff < eq_high else 1.0\n    else:\n        t_low = (mean_diff - eq_low) / se_diff\n        t_high = (mean_diff - eq_high) / se_diff\n        p_low = 1.0 - t.cdf(t_low, df)\n        p_high = t.cdf(t_high, df)\n\n    p_equivalence = max(p_low, p_high)\n\n    if p_equivalence < alpha:\n        decision = \"Equivalent\"\n        interpretation = \"Good (within equivalence bounds)\"\n    else:\n        decision = \"Not Equivalent\"\n        interpretation = \"Bad (outside equivalence bounds)\"\n\n    return {\n        \"N\": n,\n        \"mean_diff(IMP-TRUE)\": mean_diff,\n        \"p_low\": p_low,\n        \"p_high\": p_high,\n        \"p_equivalence\": p_equivalence,\n        \"Decision (TOST alpha=0.05)\": decision,\n        \"Interpretation\": interpretation\n    }\n\n\ndef equivalence_test_table(true_df, imp_df):\n    equivalence_bounds = {\n        \"meanNN (s)\": (-0.002, 0.002),\n        \"HR (bpm)\": (-0.5, 0.5),\n        \"SDNN (ms)\": (-5.0, 5.0),\n        \"RMSSD (ms)\": (-5.0, 5.0),\n        \"pNN50 (%)\": (-2.0, 2.0),\n        \"VLF (%)\": (-3.0, 3.0),\n        \"LF (%)\": (-3.0, 3.0),\n        \"HF (%)\": (-3.0, 3.0),\n        \"LF/HF\": (-0.3, 0.3)\n    }\n\n    rows = []\n    for metric, bounds in equivalence_bounds.items():\n        result = tost_paired_equivalence(\n            x_true=true_df[metric].values,\n            x_imp=imp_df[metric].values,\n            eq_low=bounds[0],\n            eq_high=bounds[1],\n            alpha=0.05\n        )\n        row = {\"Metric\": metric, \"eq_low\": bounds[0], \"eq_high\": bounds[1]}\n        row.update(result)\n        rows.append(row)\n\n    tost_df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    cols = [\n        \"Metric\",\n        \"N\",\n        \"eq_low\",\n        \"eq_high\",\n        \"mean_diff(IMP-TRUE)\",\n        \"p_low\",\n        \"p_high\",\n        \"p_equivalence\",\n        \"Decision (TOST alpha=0.05)\",\n        \"Interpretation\"\n    ]\n    return tost_df[cols]\n\n\ndef make_ttest_summary(ttest_df, alpha=0.05):\n    rows = []\n\n    for _, row in ttest_df.iterrows():\n        metric = row[\"Metric\"]\n        mean_diff = row[\"mean_diff(IMP-TRUE)\"]\n        p_value = row[\"p_value\"]\n\n        if not np.isfinite(p_value):\n            decision = \"Invalid\"\n            interpretation = \"Insufficient data\"\n        elif p_value < alpha:\n            decision = \"Significant\"\n            interpretation = \"Statistically different\"\n        else:\n            decision = \"Not Significant\"\n            interpretation = \"No statistically significant difference\"\n\n        rows.append({\n            \"Metric\": metric,\n            \"Mean Diff (IMP-TRUE)\": mean_diff,\n            \"p-value\": p_value,\n            \"Decision (alpha=0.05)\": decision,\n            \"Interpretation\": interpretation\n        })\n\n    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n\n\ndef make_combined_hrv_summary(ttest_df, tost_df, alpha=0.05):\n    rows = []\n\n    for _, trow in ttest_df.iterrows():\n        metric = trow[\"Metric\"]\n        matched_tost = tost_df[tost_df[\"Metric\"] == metric]\n\n        if len(matched_tost) == 0:\n            continue\n\n        tost_row = matched_tost.iloc[0]\n        mean_diff = trow[\"mean_diff(IMP-TRUE)\"]\n        p_value = trow[\"p_value\"]\n        q_value = trow[\"q_value(FDR_BH)\"]\n        tost_decision = tost_row[\"Decision (TOST alpha=0.05)\"]\n        tost_p = tost_row[\"p_equivalence\"]\n\n        if not np.isfinite(p_value):\n            ttest_decision = \"Invalid\"\n        elif p_value < alpha:\n            ttest_decision = \"Statistically different\"\n        else:\n            ttest_decision = \"Not statistically different\"\n\n        if tost_decision == \"Equivalent\":\n            final_decision = \"Preserved\"\n            final_interpretation = \"Good: statistically equivalent within practical HRV bounds\"\n        elif tost_decision == \"Not Equivalent\":\n            final_decision = \"Not preserved\"\n            final_interpretation = \"Bad: outside practical equivalence bounds\"\n        else:\n            final_decision = \"Invalid\"\n            final_interpretation = \"Insufficient data\"\n\n        rows.append({\n            \"Metric\": metric,\n            \"Mean Diff (IMP-TRUE)\": mean_diff,\n            \"t-test p-value\": p_value,\n            \"FDR q-value\": q_value,\n            \"t-test Decision\": ttest_decision,\n            \"TOST p-value\": tost_p,\n            \"TOST Decision\": tost_decision,\n            \"Final Decision\": final_decision,\n            \"Final Interpretation\": final_interpretation\n        })\n\n    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n\n# ============================================================\n# 20. FINAL TEST EVALUATION AND HRV ANALYSIS\n# ============================================================\n\nprint(\"\\nLoading best model...\")\nmodel.load_state_dict(torch.load(best_model_path, map_location=DEVICE))\nmodel.to(DEVICE)\nmodel.eval()\n\n# Final pointwise evaluation uses the paper-style full-sequence missing-value procedure.\n# This is different from the quick window-level validation loader.\ntest_metrics, outlier_df = evaluate_full_sequence_missing_prediction(\n    model=model,\n    all_rr_subset=test_all_rr,\n    rr_mean=rr_mean,\n    rr_std=rr_std,\n    missing_rate=MAIN_MISSING_RATE,\n    missing_type=TEST_MISSING_TYPE,\n    repeats=1,\n    window_size=WINDOW_SIZE,\n    stride=STRIDE,\n    device=DEVICE,\n    apply_clip=APPLY_PHYSIOLOGICAL_CLIP_IN_EVAL\n)\n\nprint(\"\\n================ POINTWISE TEST METRICS ================\")\nprint(f\"N missing points: {test_metrics['N_missing_points']}\")\nprint(f\"MAE_norm: {test_metrics['MAE_norm']:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"MSE_norm: {test_metrics['MSE_norm']:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"RMSE_norm: {test_metrics['RMSE_norm']:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"R2_norm: {test_metrics['R2_norm']:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"MAE_seconds: {test_metrics['MAE_seconds']:.8f}\")\nprint(f\"RMSE_seconds: {test_metrics['RMSE_seconds']:.8f}\")\nprint(f\"MAE_ms: {